{"name":"Red Hot","hex":"#dd0033","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red hot","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A frankfurter, a hot dog."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative form of red-hot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red_hot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Frank's RedHot","blocks":[{"text":"Frank's RedHot is a hot sauce made from a variety of cayenne peppers, produced by McCormick & Company. The Original blend ranks low on the Scoville scale, with 450 SHUs, while the XTRA Hot variety measures 2,000 SHUs, which is lower than Tabasco, Cholula Hot Sauce, and Tapatío, and only slightly hotter than Sriracha."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frank's_RedHot","wikidata":"Q5484813"},{"title":"Michigan hot dog","blocks":[{"text":"A Michigan hot dog, Michigan red hot, or simply \"Michigan\", is a steamed all-beef hot dog on a steamed bun topped with a meaty sauce, generally referred to as \"Michigan sauce\", and is a specialty in and around Plattsburgh, New York."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Michigan_hot_dogs_with_and_without_onions_01_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Michigan_hot_dogs_with_and_without_onions_01_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michigan_hot_dog","wikidata":"Q3141053"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/83/FranksBottleShot1.jpg/120px-FranksBottleShot1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/83/FranksBottleShot1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/83/FranksBottleShot1.jpg/120px-FranksBottleShot1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFranksBottleShot1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Cardinal.jpg/500px-Cardinal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Cardinal.jpg/500px-Cardinal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACardinal.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Cardinal_Th%C3%A9odore_Adrien_Sarr_2.JPG/500px-Cardinal_Th%C3%A9odore_Adrien_Sarr_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Cardinal_Th%C3%A9odore_Adrien_Sarr_2.JPG/500px-Cardinal_Th%C3%A9odore_Adrien_Sarr_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACardinal_Th%C3%A9odore_Adrien_Sarr_2.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Magdalena_Frackowiak.jpg/500px-Magdalena_Frackowiak.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wi